  src/shared/error-handler.ts
  src/shared/errors.test.ts
  src/shared/errors.ts
  → Register the error handler in the file that creates your Hono app, with `app.onError(errorHandler)`.
  → Add the Prisma client the repository imports with `cuilo add backend/database`, unless `src/shared/database.ts` already exports it.
  → Add `model StatusBadge` to `schema.prisma` with `id String @id @default(uuid())`, `name String`, `createdAt DateTime @default(now())` and `updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt`, then run `prisma migrate dev --name add-status-badges` and `prisma generate`.
  → Create the `status_badges` table with `drizzle-kit generate`, then `drizzle-kit migrate`.
  → Mount the routes in the file that creates your Hono app, with `app.route("/status-badges", statusBadgeRoutes(new StatusBadgeService(new DrizzleStatusBadgeRepository(db))))`, where `db` is your Drizzle database, such as the one `cuilo add backend/database` writes to `src/shared/database.ts`.
  → Mount the routes in the file that creates your Hono app, with `app.route("/status-badges", statusBadgeRoutes(new StatusBadgeService(new PrismaStatusBadgeRepository(prisma))))`, where `prisma` is the client from `src/shared/database.ts`.
