resource · axum (orm)
  src/error.rs
  src/status_badges/mod.rs
  src/status_badges/model.rs
  src/status_badges/repository.rs
  src/status_badges/routes.rs
  src/status_badges/service.rs
  → Declare the module with `mod error;` in `src/main.rs`.
  → Declare the module with `mod status_badges;` in `src/main.rs`.
  → Create the `status_badges` table with `sqlx migrate add create_status_badges`, writing `CREATE TABLE status_badges (id uuid PRIMARY KEY, name text NOT NULL, created_at timestamptz NOT NULL, updated_at timestamptz NOT NULL)`, then apply it with `sqlx migrate run`.
  → Nest the routes before your router's layers with `.nest("/status-badges", status_badges::routes(Arc::new(StatusBadgeService::new(PgStatusBadgeRepository::new(pool)))))`, importing them from `status_badges`, where `pool` is your `PgPool`, such as the one `database::connect()` from `cuilo add backend/database` returns.
